/// A resource group whose text ends right after the `=`: the `[` that opens the group is not
/// there, so the parser reports the bracket it was looking for and leaves the tree without it.
/// Before the declaration took whatever token stood there, which at the end of the text is the
/// terminal token: that token then stood in the tree twice - once as the bracket and once as the
/// end of the Program node - and `camel-parsecheck fuzz` reported "the leaves of the tree are not
/// the tokens of the text". This is that input, written down instead of drawn from a seed.
module syntax_resource_group_open

resource a =